# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment / secrets
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env.json
*.key
*.pem
secrets/
tess-secrets/
.claude/tess-secrets/

# Encrypted identity / vault material (never publish)
# The vault DIRECTORY is intentionally NOT fully ignored — .gitkeep and vault.registry.json
# must be committable (public scaffold). Only the actual secret material is ignored:
.claude/vault/vault.age
.claude/vault/vault.recipients
.claude/vault/identity.age
clients/*/.vault/
# Catch any stray age blobs or identity files anywhere in the tree
**/vault.age
**/identity.age

# operator/ stubs contain injected identity — a pasted secret there could be committed
# Block the dir itself but keep the template (never_touch in manifest already covers it)
# Note: the framework ships operator/ stubs blank; real content is user-space only
operator/secrets
operator/*.secret

# DATA-LEAK-SAFETY (issue #92): operator/** reconciled with the manifest's
# never_touch entry ("operator/**": "user-authored identity & context").
# operator/* below is a belt-and-suspenders superset of the two lines above —
# it also blocks operator/profile.json, which the create-tess wizard
# (writeProfile() in create-tess/src/keystone.js) unconditionally overwrites
# with REAL identity (operator_name, telegram_channel, ...) during onboarding,
# BEFORE any git commit happens in a freshly `git init`'d instance.
#
# Deliberate asymmetry, documented (PR data-leak-safety hardening):
#   - operator/profile.json gets NO `!` re-include. It is the one file that
#     is always programmatically overwritten with real PII. The copy already
#     tracked in THIS repo's own history (a harmless generic default —
#     {"operator_name": "Operator", ...}) stays tracked only via git's
#     "already-tracked files survive a new ignore rule" behavior, never via
#     an override — so a FRESH install (git init, empty history, this same
#     .gitignore copied verbatim by create-tess's scaffolder) never tracks
#     the real value written over it.
#   - The 4 static doc-template stubs below ARE re-included: no onboarding
#     code path (create-tess/src/keystone.js bake()) ever writes to them —
#     they ship with placeholder text ("<your build command>",
#     "<your-dm-chat-id>") the operator hand-edits later, same shipped-
#     scaffold role as clients/_template/** below.
operator/*
!operator/build-facts-stub.md
!operator/identity-stub.md
!operator/org-channels.md
!operator/user-profile.md

# DATA-LEAK-SAFETY (issue #92): the append-first customization shadow layer
# (spec §5 Layer 2) — hard-guarded in the write-gate (check_manifest_write_gate
# Step 3c) but, until now, absent from .gitignore entirely.
*.local.md
**/*.local.md

# DATA-LEAK-SAFETY (issue #92): reconciled with the remaining never_touch
# entries that carry real per-instance data risk (not merely "tessctl must
# not manage this" — actual private content). `missions/**` mirrors the
# kb/wiki/* pattern below: the manifest's own note calls it "same fenced-off
# treatment as kb/**" — per-mission records (mission.md, verdicts/, retries/)
# can describe real client/business work in a live instance; only the
# hand-authored convention doc (missions/README.md) is a shipped template.
missions/*
!missions/README.md
# UPGRADE-NOTES.md: written by `tessctl update` with per-instance upgrade
# detail; not shipped, not currently tracked, but should never be committed.
UPGRADE-NOTES.md
# .mcp.json: MCP server configuration commonly embeds API keys/tokens
# directly in JSON — same secret-risk class as .env, not currently tracked.
.mcp.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dependencies / build artifacts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/

# Agent Receipt demo output — generated by examples/receipt-demo/run_demo.sh
# using ephemeral, test-only GPG keys. Never committed (see the demo's own
# README "Never real keys").
examples/receipt-demo/.output/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS / editor cruft
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code local overrides
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
channels/
.claude/channels/
.remember/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# iCloud / no-sync directories
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.nosync/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tessctl engine runtime state (committed: .tess/core, .tess/bin, tess.lock)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.tess/snapshots/*
!.tess/snapshots/.gitkeep
.tess/staging/*
!.tess/staging/.gitkeep
.tess/conflicts/
.tess/modified.json
# Goal #8: mission trace log — the no-mission-id fallback path only
# (missions/<id>/trace.jsonl is a mission-record artifact, same bucket as
# missions/<id>/verdicts/**, and is NOT ignored here).
.tess/trace/runs/*
!.tess/trace/runs/.gitkeep
.tess/update.lock

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phase 0.1 — cross-harness shared-brain state root (docs/STATE_LAYER.md).
# .tess/state/** as a whole is instance DATA (tess.manifest.json never_touch
# + the publish-clean deny set already block it from ever reaching a commit
# regardless of this file). The publish-clean gate is itself a PRE-COMMIT
# hook (`tessctl gate install-hooks`) — opt-in, not guaranteed installed on
# every clone or re-init. Without a content-level ignore here, a plain
# `git add -A` on an instance that never ran that hook would silently STAGE
# real memory/tasks/ledger data (issue #110, found reviewing #105 — the
# "can never leak regardless of gitignore state" claim in
# docs/STATE_LAYER.md overclaimed until this block covered all four
# subdirs, not just locks/). All four `.tess/state/**` subdirs now get the
# same content-ignore treatment as the `kb/wiki/**` / `missions/**` /
# `operator/**` precedent buckets below: structurally invisible to
# `git add`, hook-independent.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.tess/state/locks/*
!.tess/state/locks/.gitkeep
.tess/state/memory/*
!.tess/state/memory/.gitkeep
.tess/state/tasks/*
!.tess/state/tasks/.gitkeep
.tess/state/ledger/*
!.tess/state/ledger/.gitkeep

# Issue #131 — SKILL DRAFT SCAFFOLD (a FIFTH `.tess/state/**` subsystem,
# same fence as the four above). `.tess/state/skills/*` matches the
# `drafts/` directory as a single top-level entry, which ignores its
# entire subtree (every generated `<slug>/SKILL.md` + `provenance.json`)
# without a nested per-file pattern.
.tess/state/skills/*
!.tess/state/skills/.gitkeep

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Knowledge base content is operator/client data — keep structure, ignore content
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
kb/raw/*
!kb/raw/.gitkeep
kb/lint/*
!kb/lint/.gitkeep
# wiki: ignore ALL content, keep only the section-dir placeholders.
#
# DATA-LEAK-SAFETY (issue #92): kb/wiki/index.md and kb/wiki/log.md were
# PREVIOUSLY explicitly un-ignored here (`!kb/wiki/index.md`, `!kb/wiki/log.md`)
# despite kb/** being in the manifest's never_touch list. That override is
# REMOVED. log.md is the file Tess appends real mission/client entries to over
# the life of a live instance (see kb/wiki/log.md's own "Chronological record
# of internal missions" format) — not a static template; index.md is
# Tess-maintained the same way. Both now fall under the general `kb/wiki/*`
# ignore below, same treatment as every other kb/wiki subdirectory.
#
# This repo's own copies of these two files (harmless "No missions logged
# yet." scaffold placeholders) remain tracked here via git's "already-tracked
# survives a new ignore rule" behavior — NOT via a `!` override — so a FRESH
# instance (create-tess `git init`s empty, this .gitignore copied verbatim)
# never tracks whatever real content accumulates in its own copy.
kb/wiki/*
!kb/wiki/concepts/
!kb/wiki/missions/
!kb/wiki/people/
!kb/wiki/synthesis/
kb/wiki/concepts/*
!kb/wiki/concepts/.gitkeep
kb/wiki/missions/*
!kb/wiki/missions/.gitkeep
kb/wiki/people/*
!kb/wiki/people/.gitkeep
kb/wiki/synthesis/*
!kb/wiki/synthesis/.gitkeep

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real client folders are operator data — only the template is shipped
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
clients/*
!clients/_template/
